gpu_dirty_memory: one gatherer at a time (off by default)

Core patch. Paths are the submodule's. Applies on core16 alone.

Source: Frizti/Lichii 7e1d645557 (Lichii #138, by Paulo Tumabing), the memory part only.

EDEN_NX2_GATHER_LOCK=1. Gather swaps front_buffer under guard, then walks it with no lock. Two
gatherers can swap or clear it while the other walks it, handing the buffer cache a garbage address.
Lichii saw this crash in MemoryTracker::IteratePages on a movie in Final Fantasy Resonance. There the
second gatherer was a video decode read; core16 lacks that call. Ours could only be a sync request
and a fence running together on the split's two threads, which is not proven to happen. No console
crash has been traced to this.

Changed from the source: off by default, there always on.

Runs on the PS5: same core path.
Hang: the lock is held across the callback, which takes the texture and buffer cache mutexes. Read,
not run: no InvalidateGPUCache caller in core16 holds either mutex (fence manager, gpu.cpp, puller,
Maxwell3D, query cache's SignalFence), SignalFence drops its guard first, and the callback's texture,
buffer and pipeline calls show no gather. Keep it that way: a new gather under a cache mutex would
be a lock inversion, so a freeze.
Pool memory: none.
Checked: applies on core16. PS5-target syntax compile of a file that calls Gather, no errors; a planted
error proved the patched header was the one compiled. Lock order read, not run. Not run on the console.

Co-authored-by: Paulo Tumabing <85124994+Shrxmy@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/src/core/gpu_dirty_memory_manager.h b/src/core/gpu_dirty_memory_manager.h
--- a/src/core/gpu_dirty_memory_manager.h
+++ b/src/core/gpu_dirty_memory_manager.h
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 
 #include <atomic>
 #include <bit>
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <functional>
 #include <mutex>
 #include <utility>
@@ -48,6 +49,16 @@
     }
 
     void Gather(std::function<void(PAddr, size_t)>& callback) {
+        // EDEN_NX2_GATHER_LOCK=1: one gatherer at a time, so none can swap or clear front_buffer
+        // while another walks it. A function-local static: env.txt is read in main.
+        static const bool lock_gathers = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_GATHER_LOCK");
+        return value != nullptr && value[0] == '1';
+    }();
+        std::unique_lock gather_lk(gather_guard, std::defer_lock);
+        if (lock_gathers) {
+            gather_lk.lock();
+        }
         {
             std::scoped_lock lk(guard);
             TransformAddress t = current.exchange(default_transform, std::memory_order_relaxed);
@@ -115,6 +126,7 @@
 
     std::atomic<TransformAddress> current{};
     std::mutex guard;
+    std::mutex gather_guard;
     std::vector<TransformAddress> back_buffer;
     std::vector<TransformAddress> front_buffer;
 };
